# Line endings.
#
# This project has been edited from Windows throughout and every file in it is CRLF. Normalising on
# checkout keeps it that way when a tool or an editor on another platform writes LF - the Python
# helpers under tools/ were added from a Linux-like environment and arrived with LF, which git then
# warned about on every commit.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Binary types that must never be line-ending converted. The map images are licensed art and the
# exported PNGs are evidence used to verify measurements, so corrupting a byte of either would be
# worse than a cosmetic diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary

# Keep patch and diff output readable rather than treating it as text to convert.
*.patch -text
